# ASafariM Knowledge (learn.asafarim.site): a Next.js server at os-knowledge:3000 (apps/knowledge). NOT a site file of
# its own: the full deploy (deploy/vps-deploy.sh) appends this block to sites/asafarim-os.caddy (after Flow's, when
# Flow is deployed too), and publishes the result under the same edge site name (asafarim-os), ONLY when the commit
# has apps/knowledge/.env.production.age and os-knowledge is running and ready. Without that file the published site
# file is what it was before: a Caddy site for a host with no container would only turn a TLS error into a 502.
#
# Public: published articles are for everyone and may be indexed. The studio sends its own X-Robots-Tag (noindex) and
# Cache-Control (private, no-store) from the app (apps/knowledge/next.config.ts), so they are not set here. No
# Content-Security-Policy here for the same reason as docs: Next's pages need their inline scripts. `defer` makes the
# edge's values replace the upstream's instead of sending each header twice.
learn.asafarim.site {
  header {
    defer
    Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
    X-Content-Type-Options nosniff
    Referrer-Policy strict-origin-when-cross-origin
    X-Frame-Options DENY
    -Server
    -X-Powered-By
  }
  reverse_proxy os-knowledge:3000
}
